{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bayesian classification bayesian classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md","fileName":"Bayesian Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bayesian Classification","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Bayesian Information Fusion]] · [[Classification and Decision Trees]] · [[Statistical Learning and Validation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Bayesian Information Fusion","Classification and Decision Trees","Statistical Learning and Validation","bayesianprogramming.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bayesian classification bayesian classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md","fileName":"Bayesian Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bayesian Classification","heading":"Bayesian Classification","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Bayesian classification estimates a class variable from observed attributes by computing the posterior probability of each class. The description models how attribute values depend on the class and may include priors or dependencies among attributes.\n\nThe full posterior preserves ambiguity among classes. A later decision can choose the most probable class or use costs that distinguish different kinds of classification error.\n\nFor labeled data, the classifier combines class priors with feature likelihoods and selects the class with the largest posterior score. A naive Bayes implementation assumes conditional independence among attributes; this reduces computation but requires smoothing when an unseen feature-class combination would otherwise force a zero product.\n\nThe source presents the general Bayes decision boundary: for a given predictor vector, assign the class with the largest conditional probability. Practical learning methods approximate this unknown probability from training data rather than observing the true boundary directly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Bayesian Information Fusion","Classification and Decision Trees","Statistical Learning and Validation","bayesianprogramming.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bayesian classification bayesian classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bayesian Classification.md","fileName":"Bayesian Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bayesian Classification","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[bayesianprogramming.pdf]]\n\n[[clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Bayesian Information Fusion","Classification and Decision Trees","Statistical Learning and Validation","bayesianprogramming.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}